    story: Laura Frostwind was born into a navigator family, where ropes, tides, and returning alive mattered more than stories about courage. As a child, Laura Frostwind lived through the temple bell chores, learning ritual calm, chores, fasting, and the value of repetition. As a young adult, Laura Frostwind worked through a dojo door guard, sweeping floors, correcting stances, and stealing lessons from the edge of the mat. They enter the dojo to stand on the mat as a fighter.
